# Medusa Fork — Migration Conventions

## MIGRATION DECISION LOG (required)

Every migration file must start with this comment block:

```ts
/**
 * MIGRATION DECISION LOG
 * Reason: <why — reference PRD-fork-setup.md section or task ID>
 * Changes: <list of tables/columns added, modified, or removed>
 * Reversible: Yes — down() <describe what it does>
 * Fields derived from: <DML model file or PRD task>
 */
```

## `store_id` + RLS always together

When a migration adds `store_id` to a table, it must also enable RLS and create the `tenant_isolation` policy in the same migration:

```ts
// ✅ Complete pattern
await queryRunner.query(`ALTER TABLE medusa.product ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS store_id text DEFAULT ''`)
await queryRunner.query(`UPDATE medusa.product SET store_id = 'store_01KG0VBTT0714XV2CCTEBRVC47' WHERE store_id = ''`)
await queryRunner.query(`ALTER TABLE medusa.product ALTER COLUMN store_id SET NOT NULL`)
await queryRunner.query(`ALTER TABLE medusa.product ALTER COLUMN store_id DROP DEFAULT`)
await queryRunner.query(`CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_product_store_id ON medusa.product (store_id)`)
await queryRunner.query(`ALTER TABLE medusa.product ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`)
await queryRunner.query(`ALTER TABLE medusa.product FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`)
await queryRunner.query(`
  CREATE POLICY tenant_isolation ON medusa.product
    USING (store_id = current_setting('app.tenant_id', true))
`)

// ❌ Adding store_id without RLS leaves the table unprotected
await queryRunner.query(`ALTER TABLE medusa.product ADD COLUMN store_id text NOT NULL`)
```

## `down()` is not optional

Every migration must implement a complete `down()`:

```ts
// ✅
async down(queryRunner: QueryRunner): Promise<void> {
  await queryRunner.query(`DROP POLICY IF EXISTS tenant_isolation ON medusa.product`)
  await queryRunner.query(`ALTER TABLE medusa.product DISABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`)
  await queryRunner.query(`DROP INDEX IF EXISTS idx_product_store_id`)
  await queryRunner.query(`ALTER TABLE medusa.product DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS store_id`)
}

// ❌ Empty down() silently breaks rollback
async down(): Promise<void> {}
```

## Never target production

Migrations are only run locally (`pnpm migration:run`) unless the user gives explicit written instruction to target staging or production.
